Implemented `jpath/jpath.go` with `Query(doc any, path string) ([]any, error)`:

- **Parser**: requires leading `$`; parses `.name` (ident `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*`), `.*`/`[*]` wildcards, `["key"]` with only `\"`/`\\` escapes, signed `[N]` indices, and `..name` recursive descent. Any deviation (whitespace, `$.`, `$[1`, `$["x]`, `$.1abc`, `$[abc]`, unsupported escapes, etc.) → non-nil error + nil result.
- **Evaluation**: each step maps the node list; non-applicable steps (missing key, OOB/negative index, wrong type) emit nothing — never an error. Object wildcard values are ordered by key ascending; `..name` walks pre-order (own match first, then children; object children by key) and descends into matched values. Non-matching queries return an empty non-nil slice; `$` returns `[doc]`.

Verified against the provided test plus a temporary ~40-case sanity suite (negative indices, escapes, key ordering, recursion, malformed paths, scalar/null docs), since removed.
